A||||6||MD_Fiero||Where to find power window/locks for a 86 2m4.....||||1||
Z||000000||MD_Fiero||08-10-2001||12:55 AM||||ive looked, and looked..but i cant find any kits?? can someone help me!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> TIA||||reg||1
Z||000001||mbramble||08-10-2001||08:02 AM||||Try here: <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierowarehouse/electrical.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fierowarehouse/electrical.html</A>   or<BR>here <A HREF="http://www.gscustom.com/power.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.gscustom.com/power.htm</A> <P>You can also try the local wrecker yards to see if you can find a car with the power options, remove them and install them on your car.  If you find one and have questions about what you need, drop me a note, I have done it a couple of times now.<P>Also check in the Mall section and look for Chris Pond (user name Pondski).  He may have the items you need to convert your car and he's a great guy to deal with....<P>Mike<P>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Carrolles||08-10-2001||08:07 AM||||It's best to get the workings out of a donor Fiero.||||reg||1
Z||000003||MD_Fiero||08-10-2001||02:39 PM||||Ok, cool thanks  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">...yes shur...can you tell me what all i need from a donor?(at the j/y)||||reg||1
Z||000004||goldiron||08-12-2001||01:45 AM||||If you find a donor car at the j/y take the entire doors home. I got two for $80. Much easier drilling out all the rivets with doors laid flat on your garage floor, not to mention teasing the power window regulator out. Check archives for removing doors. The michigan club site has good upgrade instructions. You need the window switches, connectors and switch plate from center console, along with the doors.  New window and door switches available from fiero store as switches in j/y were junk.  Take the lock relay and connector which is located near the chime relay over passenger foot well next to door. Everywhere pull as much wire out with connectors as possible.  Upgrade isn't difficult,just time consuming.||||reg||7
Z||000005||Songman||08-12-2001||02:08 AM||||I'm just gonna replace my entire doors! Much easier than taking home doors to gut too! Wish I could find both for $80 though. Cheapest I have found has been $75 each and I thought that was a good deal.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||7
Z||000006||862M4inCA||08-13-2001||10:50 AM||||I agree I think just a complete dorr swap is less hassle, and if you think about it you already have all the hardware mounted the way it should be in the donor door. Of course my suggestion would be that if you are going with both window and lock operations to definately find one with both already in it. OH, and VERY important that you transfer the lock cylinders. Wouldn't be much fun to get the new doors on your car just to find that your door key doesn't work.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
